133-## Do-Nothing Option
134-
135-The GoDoc half needs nothing — it is already done. The only cost of doing nothing is onboarding: a new agent author reads a "Related" list pointing at four paths that do not exist in this repository and must open the Go source to find where the dependency wiring and the step framework live. The fix is one README section, which is cheaper than the confusion it removes; deferring it buys nothing and the confusion recurs with every template copy.
=== spec ACs ===
34:## Acceptance Criteria
36:- [ ] AC1 — README contains exactly one `## Package layout` heading whose next `##` heading is `## Related`, and the section body carries a `pkg/factory` line naming at least two of the deliverer/sync-producer/agent-provider responsibilities and a `pkg/steps` line naming at least two of plan/execute/verify. Evidence: file-content grep — the AC1 assertion block in Verification prints `OK` and exits 0; a bare `touch`, a bare path list, a one-token stub line, a section placed after `## Related`, or a section inserted anywhere earlier than immediately before `## Related` prints `FAIL` and exits 1.
37:- [ ] AC2 — the GoDoc coverage check passes: every exported top-level declaration and every method on an exported receiver type under `pkg/`, `cmd/`, and the root `main.go` (test files excluded) is immediately preceded by a `//` comment line. Evidence: exit code 0 plus the stdout line `documented_exported=24` (or a larger count); a removed or blank-line-detached doc comment exits 1 and prints the offending `file:line`, while a scan finding fewer than 24 exported declarations exits 1 with only the `documented_exported=<n>` line.
38:- [ ] AC3 — `make precommit` exits 0. Evidence: exit code.
39:- [ ] AC4 — the change touches no file other than `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, and this spec. Evidence: negative file diff — `git status --porcelain` lists only those paths.
40:- [ ] AC5 — `CHANGELOG.md` carries an `## Unreleased` section with one entry naming the README package-layout section. Evidence: `grep -n '^## Unreleased' CHANGELOG.md` returns ≥1 match and the entry below it names `Package layout`.
52:GoDoc regression lock (AC2). Run from the repository root. It inspects every non-test Go file under `pkg/` and `cmd/`, requires each exported declaration to sit directly under a `//` comment line, counts what it inspected, and fails if the count drops below the 24 present at v0.2.9 — so deleting or emptying a package cannot pass it:
79:README section assertions (AC1):
93:CHANGELOG assertion (AC5):
118:- Whether the section is a bullet list or a table row per package is the implementer's choice, constrained by the AC1 assertion block.
126:| The section is appended after `## Related`, placed at the end of the README, or inserted anywhere earlier than immediately before `## Related` | AC1 exits 1 with `FAIL: layout heading missing, duplicated, or after Related` or `FAIL: layout section is not immediately before Related` | Move the section to immediately before `## Related`; re-run the AC1 block and confirm `OK` with exit 0 |
127:| The section lists the two paths without describing them, or gives each a single keyword | AC1 exits 1 with `FAIL: pkg/factory line missing wiring description` (or the `pkg/steps` variant) | Add the one-line description naming each package's responsibility (two tokens minimum), then re-run the AC1 block |
128:| `make format` inside `make precommit` rewrites a Go file under `pkg/`, `cmd/`, or the root `main.go` — import order, line wrapping, or a comment detached by a blank line | AC4 fails and lists the path; the GoDoc check additionally prints that `file:line` and exits 1 when a comment was detached | `git checkout -- <path>` to drop the formatting-only rewrite, then re-run `make precommit` and the check |
129:| `make precommit` fails after its `generate` target rewrote `mocks/` or `go mod tidy` touched `go.mod`/`go.sum` | AC4 fails on the leftover modifications | `git checkout -- mocks go.mod go.sum`, then re-run `make precommit` |
131:| `make precommit` fails inside an unrelated target that needs the network (tool download, vulnerability database) | AC3 cannot be evaluated; the failing target and its output are recorded | Re-run `make precommit` once; if it fails again, report the failing target rather than editing Go source to work around it |
